{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally and the Job Inquiry"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Breaking into the Field"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Consonant Blends - The <span class=\"strong\">spr</span> Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Consonant clusters like /spr/ can occur at the beginning of a word in English. <br/><br/>Practice blending the sound from one consonant sound into the next without adding a vowel sound in between."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the following words aloud."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spring\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprawl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spread\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spray\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprint\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"springboard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprinkler\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was sprinting towards the ball, but then I tripped in some mud and sprawled onto the field with my legs spread out like an eagle."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Now that it's spring, we play soccer outdoors."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Intonation in Long Questions  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Intonation is important in statements and in long questions. You use the rise and fall of your voice to show the listener when you are or are not finished."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In long questions, the intonation falls and then rises to show the question is not finished. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Normally, you place an extra emphasis on some important verbs, adjectives and nouns in the question. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "At the end, the intonation rises or falls, depending on whether it is a yes/no or information question."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say these sentences. Place extra emphasis on the bolded words. Be sure to notice if the question is a yes/no or information question."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You don't <span class=\"strong\">think</span> that <span class=\"strong\">computers</span> help people <span class=\"strong\">connect</span> with each other?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you <span class=\"strong\">mean</span> you don't enjoy the <span class=\"strong\">time</span> you spend <span class=\"strong\">online</span>?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Don't you <span class=\"strong\">think</span> you should try to <span class=\"strong\">adapt</span> instead?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you think it is <span class=\"strong\">difficult</span> for someone who wants to <span class=\"strong\">start</span> working in journalism to <span class=\"strong\">break into</span> the field?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How <span class=\"strong\">challenging</span> do you think it is for a <span class=\"strong\">new</span> journalist it to find <span class=\"strong\">stories</span> that appeal to a <span class=\"strong\">wide</span> audience?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sprawl"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stretch out in an unusual way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I tripped in some mud and sprawled onto the field."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about current events."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spring"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in North America, period of the year from March to June"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Now that it's spring, we play soccer outdoors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spread out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extended open, covering a large area (like open wings, arms or legs)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I tripped in some mud and fell onto the field with my legs spread out like an eagle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sprint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to run very quickly for a short time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was sprinting towards the ball when I tripped in some mud."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to trip"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fall because of something on the ground"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I tripped in some mud as I was playing soccer. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "eagle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a large predatory bird, often used as a symbol because of its wide wings"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I sprawled onto the field with my legs spread out like an eagle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to break into the field"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to start working in an area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As a new journalist, is it difficult to break into the field?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le15ob04aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le15ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, choose a field of work, like acting in movies, business or medicine."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose roles. One person thinks it is easy to break into this field. The other person thinks it is difficult."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Before you start the role-play, plan your ideas separately. Try to think of 3 - 4 reasons for your opinion. Do not talk about them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write key words to help you give your opinion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Complete the role-play. Make sure you use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIn my opinion ...\u201d</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\u201cI don't think ...\u201d</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try to keep the conversation going for 5 minutes."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write key words about a career field."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I engage in a role-play about a career field."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use appropriate expressions to give my opinion."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can say and use the sound <span class=\"italic\">spr</span>."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can use proper intonation in long questions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can exchange opinions about jobs and work."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What fields are easy to start worki